Package: codoc
Version: @VERSION@
Section: science
Priority: optional
Architecture: amd64
Depends: python3 (>= 3.10), python3-venv, python3-pip
Recommends: python3.10, rsync, wget, unzip
Maintainer: Moisés Maia <moimaian@gmail.com>
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Homepage: https://github.com/moimaian/CODOC
Description: Multi-target molecular docking platform (AutoDock Vina / Vina-GPU)
 CODOC is a PyQt5-based graphical tool that automates multi-target virtual
 screening: preparation of ligands (Open Babel or RDKit with Meeko) and of
 targets (ADFRsuite, PDB2PQR/PROPKA), druggability filtering, grid box
 definition (manual, from a co-crystallized ligand or by P2Rank pockets),
 molecular docking on CPU (AutoDock Vina 1.2.5) or GPU (Vina-GPU 2.1),
 redocking validation by RMSD, and result tables, plots and a final report.
 .
 This package installs the application files to /opt/codoc and a menu
 launcher. On first run, CODOC itself creates an isolated Python 3.10
 virtual environment at ~/.venv/CODOC and installs its own scientific
 dependencies (RDKit, Meeko, etc.) into it — this package does not do that
 as root during installation, by design (see packaging/deb/README.md).
